knowledge:[
  {id:"k1", folder:"Getting Started", title:"Creative request to approval — how work flows", by:"zein", ago:10*D, fav:true, pinned:true, body:"# How work flows\n\nEvery piece of work follows the same path so nobody has to ask where something is.\n\n1. **Request** — Marketing submits a creative request.\n2. **Brief** — a lead turns it into a structured creative brief.\n3. **Production** — the assignee uploads versions.\n4. **Review** — reviewer approves or requests revision with specific feedback.\n5. **Delivery** — approved files go to the delivery bucket.\n\n> Rule of thumb: if it is not in ZenCrevia, it is not a task."},
  {id:"k2", folder:"Compliance SOP", title:"What compliance will reject", by:"zein", ago:12*D, fav:true, pinned:true, body:"# What compliance will reject\n\nSend it to the **Compliance** stage before it goes anywhere public. These come back every single time:\n\n1. Any number presented as an expected return.\n2. The words *pasti*, *dijamin*, *bebas risiko*, or an equivalent in English.\n3. A screenshot of a real account P/L, even blurred.\n4. A risk disclaimer under 11pt, or below 4.5:1 contrast.\n5. Missing regulator lockup in the footer.\n6. Testimonials that mention a profit amount.\n\nWhen in doubt: describe the tool, not the outcome."},
  {id:"k2b", folder:"Design SOP", title:"Review etiquette", by:"laura", ago:30*D, fav:false, pinned:false, body:"# Review etiquette\n\n- Review within **one working day**.\n- Use image annotations for placement feedback; use comments for direction.\n- One revision round per version — batch your feedback.\n- Internal comments stay internal. Stakeholder-visible comments are written for the stakeholder.\n- Anything public-facing goes through **Compliance** after internal review, never instead of it."},
  {id:"k3", folder:"Brand Guidelines", title:"Color", by:"laura", ago:60*D, fav:true, pinned:false, body:"# Color\n\nPrimary **HSB Navy** `#0B2A5B`. Support with signal blue `#1F4FD8` and paper `#F4F6FA`.\n\n- Green `#16A34A` and red `#DC2626` are **market colours only** — up and down. Never use them decoratively.\n- The risk disclaimer must clear 4.5:1 contrast on whatever it sits on. No exceptions."},
  {id:"k4", folder:"Brand Guidelines", title:"Typography", by:"zein", ago:5*D, fav:false, pinned:false, body:"# Typography\n\nHeadlines: **Poppins** (600/700).\nBody: **Inter**.\nNumbers in charts and price tables: **Inter tabular figures**, always.\n\n| Role | Size | Leading |\n|---|---|---|\n| Display | 64–96 | 0.95 |\n| Headline | 32–48 | 1.05 |\n| Body | 15–17 | 1.5 |\n| Disclaimer | 11 min | 1.35 |"},
  {id:"k5", folder:"Design SOP", title:"Photography", by:"sarah", ago:45*D, fav:false, pinned:false, body:"# Photography\n\nReal people at a desk or on a phone, cool daylight. No stacks of cash, no supercars, no stock “success” imagery — compliance rejects all three on sight. Charts are illustration; never screenshot a real account."},
  {id:"k6", folder:"File Naming", title:"Naming convention", by:"zein", ago:90*D, fav:true, pinned:false, body:"# Naming convention\n\n`{project}-{deliverable}-v{n}.{ext}`\n\nExamples:\n\n- `hsbpro-hero-v2.psd`\n- `standee-branch12-v1.ai`\n\nFinal files get the suffix `-FINAL` and are copied to the S3 delivery bucket."},
  {id:"k7", folder:"Export Guidelines", title:"Web and app exports", by:"rizky", ago:25*D, fav:false, pinned:false, body:"# Web and app exports\n\n- Hero: 1920×720 WebP, ≤ 350 KB\n- App splash: 1170×2532 PNG @2x\n- Always export a 2x and 1x variant; name them `@2x` and `@1x`."},
  {id:"k8", folder:"Social Specs", title:"Instagram and TikTok", by:"andi", ago:15*D, fav:false, pinned:true, body:"# Instagram and TikTok\n\n| Format | Size | Safe zone |\n|---|---|---|\n| Feed | 1080×1350 | 80 px sides |\n| Story / Reels | 1080×1920 | 250 px top, 340 px bottom |\n| TikTok | 1080×1920 | 300 px bottom |"},
  {id:"k9", folder:"Video SOP", title:"Reels and TikTok delivery", by:"andi", ago:7*D, fav:false, pinned:false, body:"# Reels and TikTok delivery\n\n- Master: ProRes 422, 1080×1920, 30 fps.\n- Deliver H.264 ≤ 30 MB with burned-in captions.\n- Sound-on hook in the first second; logo end card 1.5 s."},
  {id:"k10", folder:"Getting Started", title:"Weekly creative sync", by:"zein", ago:7*D, fav:false, pinned:false, body:"# Weekly creative sync\n\nMonday 10:00. Agenda comes from the dashboard: overdue first, then needs review, then workload."}
],
